    <string name="about_text">Nuance is free software (GPL-3.0 licence). Source code: github.com/j3ffx/nuance\n\nModels and references: Machado, Oliveira and Fernandes (2009); Viénot, Brettel and Mollon (1999); Brettel, Viénot and Mollon (1997); Fidaner, Lin and Ozguven (2005); Sharma, Wu and Dalal (2005); Oklab (Björn Ottosson, 2020); Farnsworth (1947) and Vingrys and King-Smith (1988) for the hue arrangement test. Values checked against DaltonLens (public domain and MIT) and colour-science (BSD-3-Clause).\n\nLibraries: Kotlin and Compose Multiplatform, AndroidX, CameraX and the Material icons (Apache-2.0 licence).</string>
    <string name="help_intro">Nuance changes the camera image to help you tell apart the colours you confuse.</string>
    <string name="help_modes_title">The modes</string>
    <string name="help_modes">• Correct: changes colours so you can tell them apart. The slider sets the strength; the “Lightness” / “Hues” button switches between two ways of doing it.\n• One colour: keeps one colour only, the rest turns grey.\n• My view: shows how you see colours, to help someone understand.\n• Compare: the normal and the corrected image side by side, in 4 views or 2.</string>
    <string name="help_image_title">The pipette and the image</string>
    <string name="help_image">Tap a point of the image to know its real colour, and how you probably see it. Touch and hold, or “Original”, to see the image without the filter. Pinch to zoom. The pause button freezes the image: you can then zoom into it and move around.</string>
    <string name="help_photos_title">Photos and videos</string>
    <string name="help_photos">Photos and videos go to the Nuance album of your gallery, without any location. Settings → Photos and videos → “Filtered + original” also keeps the original. “Gallery” opens a photo and puts the same filters on it; “Back” brings you back.</string>
    <string name="help_profile_title">Your profile</string>
    <string name="help_profile">Your profile says which colours you confuse, and how much: one slider per type. Usually only one is affected; several can be mixed (for example protan and a little tritan), as an approximation, since no model has been validated for that. Tap your profile at the top of the camera to change it, or to save the settings you changed. Don’t know your type? “Find my profile” is a 3-minute test that suggests one.\n\nAchromatopsia (vision without colours): correction makes no sense, but the contrast, in “More settings”, can help.</string>
    <string name="help_privacy_title">Privacy</string>
    <string name="help_privacy">Images never leave the phone. No account, no statistics. The only possible connection is the update check on GitHub, off by default.</string>
    <string name="help_medical_title">Not a medical device</string>
    <string name="help_medical">Nuance doesn’t give “normal” vision and doesn’t cure anything. The test gives an indication, not a diagnosis: for one, see an eye doctor or an orthoptist.</string>
    <string name="action_help">Help</string>

    <!-- Find my profile -->
    <string name="screening_title">Find my profile</string>
    <string name="screening_intro">Three short steps, about 3 minutes: read digits hidden in dots, sort caps by colour, then spot a square slightly different from the others.</string>
    <string name="screening_conditions">For a reliable result: full brightness, indoors, no blue light filter, no night mode and no colour correction on the phone.</string>
    <string name="screening_private">Your answers and your result stay on your phone.</string>
    <string name="screening_not_medical">This test gives an indication, not a diagnosis: only an eye doctor or an orthoptist can make one. The screen isn’t calibrated and lighting changes colours, which can skew the result.</string>
